---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Copyright | Kvisl" description="Copyright, quotation, licensing, and reuse rules for Kvisl.">
  <main class="container page-main narrow-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Copyright</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated 19 September 2026</p>

    <div class="policy-copy">
      <p>Unless a page states otherwise, original <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> writing, editing, curation, page design, graphics, and other original publication material are protected by copyright and related rights.</p>

      <h2>Quotation</h2>
      <p>Reasonable quotation is permitted where allowed by law when the excerpt is proportionate, preserves context, and clearly credits the author, article title, and <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>. A link to the canonical article should be included online.</p>

      <h2>Republication and licensing</h2>
      <p>Full republication, translation, adaptation, syndication, commercial reuse, and substantial reproduction require prior written permission. Licensing starts at US$600 per article and may be higher depending on the work, <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>'s editorial and creative contribution, the original author's terms, territory, language, medium, duration, audience, and intended use.</p>
      <p>Payment alone does not create permission. A licence is effective only when <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> confirms the permitted use in writing.</p>

      <h2>Images and third-party material</h2>
      <p>Photographs, illustrations, quotations, datasets, and other third-party material may be owned or licensed separately. A licence to republish an article does not automatically include those rights unless the written licence expressly says so.</p>

      <h2>Translations and adaptations</h2>
      <p>Translations, abridgements, edited versions, audio or video adaptations, and other derivative uses require separate written approval. Approved versions must preserve the agreed attribution and may require author review.</p>

      <h2>Copyright concerns</h2>
      <p>If you believe material on the site infringes your rights, use the official Contact page and identify the work, the relevant <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> URL, your basis for claiming rights, and a reliable way to reach you. We may request additional information before acting.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
